r"""patch_L443_21_comets_room_20261026.py -- the fourteen comets on open paths join the Solar System
room, each drawn from a year before its perihelion to a year after
today, solid where it has travelled and dashed where JPL predicts it
will go; and the drawer's groups become one JPL class to a row (L-443,
slice 2, build B part 2).

Built on gallery 9223cd165422bf2616715e65ca59410b8245f9e5 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io (branch
main) and orrery 5398439591f35979c4df1791e25477ac37119b01 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery. It runs AFTER the
orrery's patch_L443_20_comets_20261026.py and the orrery's maintenance
run, committed and pushed: the website's objects mirror refuses an
entry the orrery's export has not keyed.

WHAT IT EDITS, all or nothing

    data/objects_config.json: fourteen comet entries, each a path
        (open_path); the drawer's rows one JPL class to a row: after the
        Sun, Encke-type, Jupiter-family, Halley-type comets, Comets,
        Hyperbolic comets, Interstellar objects; Aten asteroids after
        Venus; Apollo and Amor asteroids after the Spacecraft.
    tools/mirror_objects.py and its suite: open_path copied from the
        orrery's export.
    tools/gallery_cache_builder.py and its suite: a comet on an open
        path is fetched by its plan, like a spacecraft.
    gallery/assembler/: any body served positions and no elements is
        drawn as a path, a comet with its diamond; the comets' colours.
    interactive.html: the comets' text box and source line in Tony's
        approved words; the room's list a bullet for them; a name the
        orrery keys with an underscore shown with a space.
    gallery/solar_system_figures.js and its smoke: the orbit line,
        "perihelion q AU, its closest to the Sun, to aphelion Q AU, its
        farthest."
    gallery_maintenance_run.py: the live check fetches the fourteen
        positions files. tools/headless/: the driver's helper and the
        drawer walk's comets section.

HOW TO RUN

    Save it in the website folder (tonyquintanilla.github.io), open it
    in VS Code and press Run (the same as python patch_L443_21_comets_room_20261026.py from that folder).
    It asks nothing, prints an "ok" line per file, then "patch applied".
    A second run refuses. Then run the Daily Run from the dashboard, not
    the maintenance run alone: its pulls copy each comet's plan into the
    config, its build fetches the paths, and only then do the checks
    have comets to look at. Move this file into documentation\, commit
    and push. Undo before a commit is Discard Changes in GitHub Desktop.

Written October 26, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""
